{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Video Understanding \u2014 Temporal Modeling Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Frame sampler"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Uniform and dense samplers that work on a list of frames (or a video tensor)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sample_uniform(num_frames_total, T):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if num_frames_total <= T:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return list(range(num_frames_total)) + [num_frames_total - 1] * (T - num_frames_total)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    step = num_frames_total / T"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [int(i * step) for i in range(T)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sample_dense(num_frames_total, T, rng=None):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rng = rng or np.random.default_rng()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if num_frames_total <= T:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return list(range(num_frames_total)) + [num_frames_total - 1] * (T - num_frames_total)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    start = int(rng.integers(0, num_frames_total - T + 1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return list(range(start, start + T))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Both return `T` indices that you use to slice the video tensor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: A 2D+pool baseline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run a 2D ResNet-18 over every frame, average-pool features, classify."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torchvision.models import resnet18, ResNet18_Weights"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class FramePool(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, num_classes=400, pretrained=True):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        weights = ResNet18_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1 if pretrained else None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        backbone = resnet18(weights=weights)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.features = nn.Sequential(*(list(backbone.children())[:-1]))  # global avg pool kept"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.head = nn.Linear(512, num_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        # x: (N, T, 3, H, W)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        N, T = x.shape[:2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = x.view(N * T, *x.shape[2:])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        feats = self.features(x).view(N, T, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pooled = feats.mean(dim=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.head(pooled)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = FramePool(num_classes=10)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = torch.randn(2, 8, 3, 224, 224)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"output: {model(x).shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"params: {sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters()):,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Eleven million parameters, ImageNet pretrained, runs per-frame, averages, classifies. This baseline is often within 5-10 points of proper 3D models on appearance-heavy tasks \u2014 sometimes better, because it reuses a stronger ImageNet backbone."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: An I3D-style inflated 3D conv"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Turn a single 2D conv into a 3D conv by repeating weights along a new time axis."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def inflate_2d_to_3d(conv2d, time_kernel=3):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out_c, in_c, kh, kw = conv2d.weight.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    weight_3d = conv2d.weight.data.unsqueeze(2)  # (out, in, 1, kh, kw)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    weight_3d = weight_3d.repeat(1, 1, time_kernel, 1, 1) / time_kernel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    conv3d = nn.Conv3d(in_c, out_c, kernel_size=(time_kernel, kh, kw),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                        padding=(time_kernel // 2, conv2d.padding[0], conv2d.padding[1]),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                        stride=(1, conv2d.stride[0], conv2d.stride[1]),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                        bias=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    conv3d.weight.data = weight_3d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return conv3d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "conv2d = nn.Conv2d(3, 64, kernel_size=3, padding=1, bias=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "conv3d = inflate_2d_to_3d(conv2d, time_kernel=3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"2D weight shape:  {tuple(conv2d.weight.shape)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"3D weight shape:  {tuple(conv3d.weight.shape)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = torch.randn(1, 3, 8, 56, 56)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"3D output shape:  {tuple(conv3d(x).shape)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The division by `time_kernel` keeps the activation magnitudes roughly constant \u2014 important for not breaking batch-norm statistics on the first pass."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Factorised (2+1)D conv"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Split a 3D conv into a 2D (spatial) and a 1D (temporal) conv. Same receptive field, fewer parameters, better accuracy on some benchmarks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Conv2Plus1D(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, in_c, out_c, kernel_size=3):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mid_c = (in_c * out_c * kernel_size * kernel_size * kernel_size) \\"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                // (in_c * kernel_size * kernel_size + out_c * kernel_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.spatial = nn.Conv3d(in_c, mid_c, kernel_size=(1, kernel_size, kernel_size),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                                 padding=(0, kernel_size // 2, kernel_size // 2), bias=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.bn = nn.BatchNorm3d(mid_c)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.act = nn.ReLU(inplace=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.temporal = nn.Conv3d(mid_c, out_c, kernel_size=(kernel_size, 1, 1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                                  padding=(kernel_size // 2, 0, 0), bias=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.temporal(self.act(self.bn(self.spatial(x))))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "c = Conv2Plus1D(3, 64)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = torch.randn(1, 3, 8, 56, 56)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"(2+1)D output: {tuple(c(x).shape)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A full R(2+1)D network is the same as a ResNet-18 with every 3x3 conv replaced by `Conv2Plus1D`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Compute FLOPs (approximate) for FramePool with T=8 vs an I3D-style 3D ResNet with T=8. Justify why 2D+pool is 3-5x cheaper.\n2. **(Medium)** Generate a synthetic video dataset: random balls moving in random directions, labelled by direction of motion (\"left-to-right\", \"right-to-left\", \"diagonal-up\"). Train FramePool on it. Show that it achieves near-chance accuracy, proving appearance alone is insufficient for motion tasks.\n3. **(Hard)** Build an R(2+1)D-18 by replacing every Conv2d in a ResNet-18 with `Conv2Plus1D`. Inflate the first conv's weights from an ImageNet-pretrained ResNet-18. Train on the motion dataset from exercise 2 and beat FramePool."
      ]
    }
